    "updated_at": "2022-05-22T10:24:36Z",
    "body": "Bikeshedding but `.alpha` doesn't seem great here, it really sounds more like it would control the global opacity of the gradient rather than control how the values are interpolated.   \r\nI'm not sure what would be better though, maybe `.alphaPremultiplication` or `.alphaInterpolation`?  \r\n\r\nBut I even wonder if an enum is really necessary here, is there any chance this `AlphaPremutiplication` enum ever grows? Maybe a boolean `.alphaPremultiplied` would be better?\r\n\r\nAnd to keep on bikeshedding, I'd also propose that the `Method` part on the two other attributes be removed so that at least `colorInterpolation` matches the [SVG counter-part](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute/color-interpolation).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
