    "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#premultiplied-alpha-and-the-2d-rendering-context\n\n> A [CanvasRenderingContext2D](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#canvasrenderingcontext2d)'s [output bitmap](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#output-bitmap) and an [OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#offscreencanvasrenderingcontext2d)'s [output bitmap](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#output-bitmap) must use premultiplied alpha to represent transparent colors.\n\nIs there anywhere I'm missing in the spec that says that canvasGradients are unpremultiplied? Or is it just a historical quirk?\n\nI agree with @Kaiido on the first point.  I would go with `.premultipliedAlpha`, because that's generally how I see the concept described, for example:\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/apps/develop/win2d/premultiplied-alpha\n\nAlso, a boolean seems sufficient.\n\nFor the second point, CSS uses \"method\" in the name. I think it's more valuable to be in-sync with CSS than with SVG, but I could be convinced otherwise.\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#typedef-hue-interpolation-method\n\nI will get to work on this unless there is an objection here!",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
