    "created_at": "2025-02-01T02:01:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-01T02:01:58Z",
    "body": "> For the second point, CSS uses \"method\" in the name. I think it's more valuable to be in-sync with CSS than with SVG, but I could be convinced otherwise.\n\nNot that I feel strongly about this in any way, but is the \"-method\" naming there exposed anywhere in the API outside of the specs (and docs)? Given that SVG's property *is* exposed to authors, I'd assume that would make the precedent, but maybe CSS TypedOM does expose these too?",
