    "created_at": "2025-02-01T17:02:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-01T17:02:38Z",
    "body": "The one main change needs from my initial straw man is to remove \"specified\" from the `HueInterpolationMethod` enum, as it is no longer part of CSS.\n\nAs for the specific attribute names for `CanvasGradient`, I don't have strong opinions, though I agree `alpha` on its own is bad.\n\n> Is there anywhere I'm missing in the spec that says that canvasGradients are unpremultiplied? Or is it just a historical quirk?\n\n@mysteryDate, This is specified in the canvas interpolation section: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#interpolation\n\n> [...] Between each such stop, the colors and the alpha component must be linearly interpolated over the RGBA space without premultiplying the alpha value to find the color to use at that offset. [...]",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
