    "updated_at": "2025-02-01T17:34:30Z",
    "body": "> [@mysteryDate](https://github.com/mysteryDate), This is specified in the canvas interpolation section: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#interpolation\n\nThanks! Not sure how I missed that.\n\n> The one main change needs from my initial straw man is to remove \"specified\" from the HueInterpolationMethod enum, as it is no longer part of CSS.\n\nOf course, good point.\n\n@Kaiido \n> Not that I feel strongly about this in any way, but is the \"-method\" naming there exposed anywhere in the API outside of the specs (and docs)? Given that SVG's property is exposed to authors, I'd assume that would make the precedent, but maybe CSS TypedOM does expose these too?\n\nAs far as I know CSS TypedOM is not yet specced for any of the new color spaces. But they are referenced in MDN docs: \n\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/hue-interpolation-method\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color-interpolation-method\n\nI think that `color-interpolation` for SVG is part of some older spec (note the lack of spaces available), a similar property is available in CSS:\n\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color-interpolation\n\nI'm not sure why this property wasn't expanded for the new gradients, but it does seem like the specifically added `-method` in order to avoid a collision. \n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
